{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1357591-faerie-support-groups","id":1357591,"title":"Faerie Support Groups","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-29T12:47:57-08:00","id":1357591,"title":"Faerie Support Groups","content":"So here's an idea I'm working on for a chronicle:<br /> <br /> Not every town or city has a functioning freehold, but, humans being humans, people with similar beliefs will still find ways to clump together. It stands to reason that Fetches, having the ability to see through The Mask but not necessarily have any idea what it is they're actually seeing, might start seeking out others who claim to have had similar experiences, just to prove to themselves that they're not actually crazy/find validation. Fae-Touched, too, have had experiences that they can't quite quantify -- <i>especially</i> if they escaped the Hedge on their own, in areas where The Courts are weak. Add to this regular humans who have abilities like Unseen Sense or Aura Reading, who might be drawn to groups that can claim to have insight into what they're picking up, as well as those who only <i>think</i> they have these abilities. Add in some New Age nuttery, like The Law of Attraction, Near-Death Experiences, Alien &quot;Experiencers,&quot; and other woo, and you have the makings of a strange semi-cultish group.<br /> <br /> These &quot;Faerie Support Groups&quot; might be harmless cranks...until a Lost bound to one of the members wanders out of the Hedge and discovers their own Fetch or Avowed among them, or a nearby freehold goes on a Fetch-hunting expedition, or a Bridge Burner tries to publicly discredit them as part of a campaign to destroy &quot;dangerous Gentry-attracting beliefs,&quot; or a curious Gentry decides it might be funny to humor a mortal cult, or a Huntsman sees an opportunity to gain allies in his hunt...you get the picture.<br /> <br /> I'm planning on working one such group into a game, and wanted to tap into the board for ideas on what this sort of group might call itself, how they gain new members, and what sorts of dangers they might pose to isolated Lost in a rural area. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> (And yes, this is kinda-sorta based on <a href=\"https://tardis.fandom.com/wiki/LINDA\" target=\"_blank\">LINDA</a> from Doctor Who)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":25851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","user":"TheStray7","date":". 12-29-2019, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T18:17:49-08:00","id":1357655,"title":"","content":"From &quot;probablybadrpgideas.tumblr.com&quot;:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A game where you play a fetch. You don\u2019t know you\u2019re playing a fetch, you think you\u2019re playing a no-magic action game until an ogre version of you bursts out of a nearby door and throws a car at you. </div> </div> </div>I thought that it would be a great way to start a Chronicles of Darkness game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T18:52:12-08:00","id":1357658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1357591-faerie-support-groups?p=1357655#post1357655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I thought that it would be a great way to start a Chronicles of Darkness game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried that once, actually. It didn't work out particularly well. Fooling the Characters as to what they're doing is good drama, but fooling the Players themselves turns sour real fast if they don't have buy-in. If the players agree to play Fetches from the get-go, that's one thing. Springing it on them mid-game lead to a lot of bad feels.<br /> <br /> That said, yes, I can see how this would work as a good set-up for such a game. Just makes sure the characters are the ones dealing with the Bait-And-Switch, not the players themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T09:15:29-08:00","id":1357793,"title":"","content":"There are UFO groups who idolize those who have been abducted; perhaps the members of a Fae cult develop an obsession with being &quot;chosen&quot; and taken to Arcadia, as they have a wildly divergent idea of what the realm is actually like. Changeling PCs might try to convince the mortals to stop playing with fire, only for Loyalist agents to come in and smear them as enemy agents who selfishly want to keep the gifts of Glamour all to themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T12:51:19-08:00","id":1357863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1357591-faerie-support-groups?p=1357793#post1357793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are UFO groups who idolize those who have been abducted; perhaps the members of a Fae cult develop an obsession with being &quot;chosen&quot; and taken to Arcadia, as they have a wildly divergent idea of what the realm is actually like. Changeling PCs might try to convince the mortals to stop playing with fire, only for Loyalist agents to come in and smear them as enemy agents who selfishly want to keep the gifts of Glamour all to themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that as one way of going with this. The Fae-Touched members, especially, might push that particular angle, as they're the ones who got into and out of the Hedge without (much) trouble and probably don't realize how lucky they were that was the case. Plus that whole Hedge Addiction angle would be a compelling draw in this direction.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of that Ensorcelled Devoted Groupie character from the 1e book, the one who is so desperate to become special that he'd be willing to deliberately attract the attention of the Gentry. Might be a character worthy of updating to 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T13:36:24-08:00","id":1358065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1357591-faerie-support-groups?p=1357793#post1357793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are UFO groups who idolize those who have been abducted; perhaps the members of a Fae cult develop an obsession with being &quot;chosen&quot; and taken to Arcadia, as they have a wildly divergent idea of what the realm is actually like. Changeling PCs might try to convince the mortals to stop playing with fire, only for Loyalist agents to come in and smear them as enemy agents who selfishly want to keep the gifts of Glamour all to themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be honest, I can see an entire Freehold coming out of a mass escape of changelings who didn't know what was going on, conferred, and decided that the True Fae must be behind all these abduction stories - and that they are from another planet the Hedge is a hyperspace gate too, especially if the primary voices are scientists and UFOlogists. &quot;Huh, Contracts must be how we conceive of alien cybernetic sensors. Weird, but it explains why nobody's realized this is weird tech; barely looks like it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}